#: ../installation/preparation.rst:8
msgid "Preparation"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:10
msgid "You have to follow some preparation steps for Galette installation. The way to go differs on what you want to achieve."
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:15
msgid "Archive contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:17
msgid "The archive contains a single ``galette-1.3.1`` directory, laid out as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:35
msgid "What you have to copy on your server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:37
msgid "the |folder| ``galette`` directory, **mandatory**: it holds the whole application;"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:38
msgid "the |folder| ``bin`` directory, **recommended**: it provides the :doc:`command line interface <../command-line>`. It looks for the application in a ``galette`` directory next to it, so both directories must stay side by side, as they are in the archive;"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:39
msgid "the remaining files at the root of the archive are informational only; Galette does not need them."
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:44
msgid "Installation directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:46
msgid "The :ref:`installation example <installation>` extracts the archive in ``/var/www/galette-1.3.1``. This directory, which holds ``bin`` and ``galette``, is called the **installation directory** in this documentation. Unless stated otherwise, paths such as ``config`` or ``data`` are relative to its |folder| ``galette`` subdirectory: ``data`` stands for ``/var/www/galette-1.3.1/galette/data``."
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:48
msgid "Keeping the version in the directory name is not mandatory, but it makes updates easier: each release gets its own directory, next to the previous one. Updating consists in copying your configuration and data into the new directory, then pointing the web server to it - the previous version stays untouched until you remove it. See :doc:`update <update>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:50
msgid "The installation directory is created **outside** of the web server document root (often ``/var/www/html``), on purpose: only the |folder| ``galette/webroot`` directory should be reachable from the web."
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:52
msgid "If your host lets you choose the directory a domain or subdomain points to, point it to ``galette/webroot``, as explained in :ref:`web server directory exposition <installationsubdir>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:54
msgid "Otherwise (some shared hostings), copy ``galette`` in the published directory. Galette is then available at an URL like ``https://mydomain.tld/galette/``, which redirects to ``https://mydomain.tld/galette/webroot/``. The ``.htaccess`` files shipped in ``data`` directories prevent their contents from being downloaded, but only with Apache: this is less secure than exposing ``webroot`` alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:59
msgid "File permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../installation/preparation.rst:63
msgid "A commonly used hack is to give all rights to everyone recursively on the directory (``chmod 777``). This is a very very bad idea from a security point of view. Please do not use that hack, you've been warned ;)"
msgstr ""

